# .worktree-copy: manifest read by warm-worktrees.sh and by inventory-worktrees.sh
# when it classifies a dirty file as "warm" (a copy this manifest re-creates
# on every warm, as opposed to a real, uncommitted change).
#
# Format:
#   - One path per line, relative to the bare clone root.
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped.
#   - An optional second field, separated by whitespace, sets the copy mode:
#       copy             (default when the field is absent) always overwrite
#                        the destination with the source.
#       copy-if-missing  copy only when the destination does not already
#                        exist, so local edits in a worktree survive later
#                        warms.
#       link             symlink the destination to the source instead of
#                        copying, so every worktree shares one file.
#
# Never list git internals here (HEAD, config, objects, refs, worktrees,
# and similar); they live in the bare root for a different reason and
# warm-worktrees.sh does not expect to see them in this file.
#
# Common candidates (uncomment and adjust the ones this repo needs):
# .env.local
# .envrc
# .npmrc
# .tool-versions
# .mcp.json
# .claude
# .agents
# .cursor
# .kiro
# AGENTS.local.md
#
# Enabled by default, since most projects need both copied into every worktree:
.env
.local
